Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-16319) Wrong broker destinations for
 DeleteRecords requests when more than one topic is involved and the
 topics/partitions are led by different brokers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

AlexeyASF created KAFKA-16319:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Wrong broker destinations for DeleteRecords requests =
when more than one topic is involved and the topics/partitions are led by d=
ifferent brokers
                 Key: KAFKA-16319
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16319
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 3.6.1
            Reporter: AlexeyASF


h2. Context

Kafka streams applications send, time after time, {{DeleteRecords}} request=
s, via {{org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager#maybePurg=
eCommittedRecords}} method. Such requests may involve more than 1 topic (or=
 partition), and such requests are supposed to be sent to partitions' leade=
rs brokers.
=C2=A0
h2. Observed behaviour

In case when {{DeleteRecords}} request includes more than one topic (let's =
say 2 - {{topic1}} and {{{}topic2{}}}), and these topics are led by differe=
nt brokers (let=E2=80=99s say {{broker1}} and {{broker2}}=C2=A0respectively=
), the request is sent to only one broker (let=E2=80=99s say {{{}broker1{}}=
}), leading to partial=C2=A0not_leader_or_follower errors. As not the whole=
 request was successful ({{{}topic1{}}} is fine, but {{topic2}}=C2=A0is not=
), it gets retried, with the _same_ arguments, to the _same_ broker ({{{}br=
oker1{}}}), meaning the response will be partially faulty again and again. =
It also may (and does) happen that there is a =E2=80=9Cmirrored=E2=80=9D ha=
lf-faulty request - in this case, to {{{}broker2{}}}, where {{topic2}} oper=
ation is successful, but {{topic1}} operation fails.

Here=E2=80=99s an anonymised logs example from a production system (=E2=80=
=9Cdirect=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9Cmirrored=E2=80=9D requests, one after anoth=
er):
{code:java}
[AdminClient clientId=3Dworker-admin]
Sending DeleteRecordsRequestData(topics=3D[
  DeleteRecordsTopic(
    name=3D'topic1',
    partitions=3D[DeleteRecordsPartition(partitionIndex=3D5, offset=3D88017=
574)]
    ),
  DeleteRecordsTopic(
    name=3D'topic2',
    partitions=3D[DeleteRecordsPartition(partitionIndex=3D5, offset=3D24384=
1)]
)], timeoutMs=3D60000)
to broker1:PORT (id: 2 rack: RACK1). // <-- Note the broker, it's broker1
correlationId=3D42003907, timeoutMs=3D30000

[AdminClient clientId=3Dworker-admin]
Sending DeleteRecordsRequestData(topics=3D[
  DeleteRecordsTopic(
    name=3D'topic1',
    partitions=3D[DeleteRecordsPartition(partitionIndex=3D5, offset=3D88017=
574)]
  ),
  DeleteRecordsTopic(
    name=3D'topic2',
    partitions=3D[DeleteRecordsPartition(partitionIndex=3D5, offset=3D24384=
1)]
)], timeoutMs=3D60000)
to broker2:9098 (id: 4 rack: RACK2). // <-- Note the broker, here it's brok=
er2
correlationId=3D42003906, timeoutMs=3D30000 {code}
Such request results in the following response (in this case, only for the =
"direct" response):
{code:java}
[AdminClient clientId=3Dworker-admin]
Call(
  callName=3DdeleteRecords(api=3DDELETE_RECORDS),
  deadlineMs=3D...,
  tries=3D..., // Can be hundreds
  nextAllowedTryMs=3D...)
got response DeleteRecordsResponseData(
  throttleTimeMs=3D0,
  topics=3D[
    DeleteRecordsTopicResult(
      name=3D'topic2',
      partitions=3D[DeleteRecordsPartitionResult(
        partitionIndex=3D5, lowWatermark=3D-1, errorCode=3D6)]), // <-- Not=
e the errorCode 6, which is not_leader_or_follower
    DeleteRecordsTopicResult(
      name=3D'topic1',
      partitions=3D[DeleteRecordsPartitionResult(
        partitionIndex=3D5, lowWatermark=3D..., errorCode=3D0)]) // <-- Not=
e the errorCode 0, which means the operation was successful
  ]
) {code}
h2. Expected behaviour

{{DeleteRecords}} requests are sent to corresponding partitions' leaders br=
okers when more than 1 topic/partition is involved and they are led by diff=
erent brokers.
h2. Notes
 * {_}presumably{_}, introduced in 3.6.1 via [https://github.com/apache/kaf=
ka/pull/13760] .



