Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-16381) We should use a lock to protect the
 config getter in KafkaMetric
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Johnny Hsu created KAFKA-16381:
----------------------------------

             Summary: We should use a lock to protect the config getter in =
KafkaMetric
                 Key: KAFKA-16381
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16381
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Johnny Hsu
            Assignee: Johnny Hsu


In KafkaMetirc.java, the getter is=C2=A0

```
@Override
public MetricName metricName() {
return this.metricName;
}
```

and there is a setter=C2=A0

```
public void config(MetricConfig config) {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 synchronized (lock) {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.config =3D config;
=C2=A0 }
}
```

Since it's possible to set and get in the mean time, we should have lock in=
 the getter as well



