stage?

On Wed, Mar 6, 2024 at 4:02=E2=80=AFPM Andrew Schofield <
andrew_schofield_jira@outlook.com> wrote:

> Hi Ahmed,
> Looks good to me with one remaining comment.
>
> You=E2=80=99ve used:
>
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time -1 --isolation -committed
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time latest --isolation -committed
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time -1 --isolation -uncommitted
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time latest --isolation -uncommitte=
d
>
> I find the flags starting with a single - to be a bit unusual and doesn=
=E2=80=99t
> match the --time options such as =E2=80=9Clatest=E2=80=9D. I suggest:
>
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time -1 --isolation committed
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time latest --isolation committed
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time -1 --isolation uncommitted
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time latest --isolation uncommitted
>
> Or even:
>
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time -1 --isolation read-committed
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time latest --isolation read-commit=
ted
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time -1 --isolation read-uncommitte=
d
> bin/kafka-get-offsets.sh  =E2=80=A6 --time latest --isolation read-uncomm=
itted
>
> Apart from that nit, looks good to me.
>
> Thanks,
> Andrew
>
>
> > On 5 Mar 2024, at 16:35, Ahmed Sobeh <ahmed.sobeh@aiven.io.INVALID>
> wrote:
> >
> > I adjusted the KIP according to what we agreed on, let me know if you
> have
> > any comments!
> >
> > Best,
> > Ahmed
> >
> > On Thu, Feb 29, 2024 at 1:44=E2=80=AFAM Luke Chen <showuon@gmail.com> w=
rote:
> >
> >> Hi Ahmed,
> >>
> >> Thanks for the KIP!
> >>
> >> Comments:
> >> 1. If we all agree with the suggestion from Andrew, you could update t=
he
> >> KIP.
> >>
> >> Otherwise, LGTM!
> >>
> >>
> >> Thanks.
> >> Luke
> >>
> >> On Thu, Feb 29, 2024 at 1:32=E2=80=AFAM Andrew Schofield <
> >> andrew_schofield_jira@outlook.com> wrote:
> >>
> >>> Hi Ahmed,
> >>> Could do. Personally, I find the existing =E2=80=9C--time -1=E2=80=9D=
 totally horrid
> >>> anyway, which was why
> >>> I suggested an alternative. I think your suggestion of a flag for
> >>> isolation level is much
> >>> better than -6.
> >>>
> >>> Maybe I should put in a KIP which adds:
> >>> --latest (as a synonym for --time -1)
> >>> --earliest (as a synonym for --time -2)
> >>> --max-timestamp (as a synonym for --time -3)
> >>>
> >>> That=E2=80=99s really what I would prefer. If the user has a timestam=
p, use
> >>> `--time`. If they want a
> >>> specific special offset, use a separate flag.
> >>>
> >>> Thanks,
> >>> Andrew
> >>>
> >>>> On 28 Feb 2024, at 09:22, Ahmed Sobeh <ahmed.sobeh@aiven.io.INVALID>
> >>> wrote:
> >>>>
> >>>> Hi Andrew,
> >>>>
> >>>> Thanks for the hint! That sounds reasonable, do you think adding a
> >>>> conditional argument, something like "--time -1 --isolation
> -committed"
> >>> and
> >>>> "--time -1 --isolation -uncommitted" would make sense to keep the
> >>>> consistency of getting the offset by time? or do you think having a
> >>> special
> >>>> argument for this case is better?
> >>>>
> >>>> On Tue, Feb 27, 2024 at 2:19=E2=80=AFPM Andrew Schofield <
> >>>> andrew_schofield_jira@outlook.com> wrote:
> >>>>
> >>>>> Hi Ahmed,
> >>>>> Thanks for the KIP.  It looks like a useful addition.
> >>>>>
> >>>>> The use of negative timestamps, and in particular letting the user
> use
> >>>>> `--time -1` or the equivalent `--time latest`
> >>>>> is a bit peculiar in this tool already. The negative timestamps com=
e
> >>> from
> >>>>> org.apache.kafka.common.requests.ListOffsetsRequest,
> >>>>> but you=E2=80=99re not actually adding another value to that. As a =
result, I
> >>>>> really wouldn=E2=80=99t recommend using -6 for the new
> >>>>> flag. LSO is really a variant of -1 with read_committed isolation
> >> level.
> >>>>>
> >>>>> I think that perhaps it would be better to add `--last-stable` as a=
n
> >>>>> alternative to `--time`. Then you=E2=80=99ll get the LSO with
> >>>>> cleaner syntax.
> >>>>>
> >>>>> Thanks,
> >>>>> Andrew
> >>>>>
> >>>>>
> >>>>>> On 27 Feb 2024, at 10:12, Ahmed Sobeh <ahmed.sobeh@aiven.io.INVALI=
