te the
> > existing
> > > > > > > value. To handle this, you'd need to support atomic sub-do=
cument
> > > > > > > operations, which I don't see happening.
> > > > > > >
> > > > > > > 2) A common pattern is to store your configurations in git=
 or
> > something,
> > > > > > > and then apply them via PUT. Throw in some triggers or jen=
kins
> > etc, and
> > > > > > you
> > > > > > > have a more robust solution than PATCH provides.
> > > > > > >
> > > > > > > 3) For properties that change a lot, it's possible to use =
